          1019.0,
          1299.0
        ],
        [
          172.0,
          1299.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "First, don't indulge in despair, because despair leads to inertia and doing nothing means certain  $ \\underline{32} $ . Every action to save nature will improve our collective and personal futures and the only way to respond to a threat of this scale is with  $ \\underline{33} $ action rooted in headstrong optimism- Second, we need relentless focus, just like when paramedics ( 救护人员 ) arrive on a scene and use the concept of triage(伤员鉴别分类)\"to ensure the most  $ \\underline{34} $ cases get treated first. Saving the natural world needs that kind of thinking. We don't have the  $ \\underline{35} $ to do everything at once. We",
